      "message": "Hello,\n\nWe encountered a Windows host-side fastboot crash while formatting a partition:\n\n\"fastboot format data\nmke2fs 1.46.6 (1-Feb-2023)\nCreating filesystem with 2693632 4k blocks and 674624 inodes\nFilesystem UUID: be4bf24c-75df-11f1-bf1b-194a51f4d094\nSuperblock backups stored on blocks:\n32768, 98304, 163840, 229376, 294912, 819200, 884736, 1605632, 2654208\n\nAllocating group tables: done\nWriting inode tables: done\nCreating journal (16384 blocks): done\nWriting superblocks and filesystem accounting information: done\n\nlibc++abi: terminating due to uncaught exception of type std::out_of_range: basic_string\"\n\nThe issue appears to be caused by reopening the generated image without O_BINARY on Windows. Other fastboot image loading paths already use O_BINARY, but fb_perform_format() reopened the temporary formatted image with O_RDONLY only.\n\nThis change reopens the generated image with O_BINARY to keep sparse image handling binary-safe on Windows.\n\nWe verified this solution in our environment, and it resolves the issue described above.\n\nPlease review.",
